    "result_text": "The full suite is green \u2014 **69 tests run, 0 failures, 0 errors** \u2014 BUILD SUCCESS.\n\n## Summary\n\nOn a successful owner create, the pipeline now enqueues a welcome notification via the `NOTIFY` logger.\n\n**New function class** \u2014 `EnqueueWelcomeNotification.java`:\n- Uses a dedicated SLF4J logger named `NOTIFY` (same convention as `AuditOwnerCreated`'s `AUDIT` logger).\n- Reads the persisted owner via `@Val Owner` and emits one line containing the owner id and the assigned `memberId`.\n\n**Wiring** \u2014 `owners.POST.yml`:\n- Inserted an `enqueueWelcome` step between `audit` and `respond` (so it runs after `SaveOwner`, when the generated id is available), keeping it inside the same `transaction` governance as the surrounding steps.\n\nThe line emitted looks like `Welcome owner id=11 memberId=NSW2716E6609E1`, satisfying `Cp57Tests.coreEnqueuesWelcome`, which asserts a `NOTIFY` line contains both the id and the memberId.",
